{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Six years you shall sow your field.</b> Then you will be able to sow a single field by itself for six consecutive years, unlike the normal practice of working the land — for the customary practice is to leave it fallow one year and sow it the next, as our Sages of blessed memory mentioned (Bava Batra 36a)." "<b>And you shall gather in its produce.</b> Unlike the normal practice in working the land, for if one parcel is sown by itself for consecutive years it will not continue to yield its full strength."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:52.856600721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}